      "id": "qi05ial",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Types of Protected Areas in India"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "India's ecological preservation relies on designated National Parks and Wildlife Sanctuaries.",
        "Major Tiger Reserves represent targeted species protection initiatives across the country.",
        "Government Wildlife Conservation Programs provide the legislative and operational framework for biodiversity protection.",
        "Understanding the types and importance of wildlife conservation is essential for environmental governance."
      ],
      "id": "9xidpzi"
    },
    {
      "id": "9o44sbo",
      "type": "table",
      "rows": [
        {
          "isHeader": true,
          "cells": [
            "<p><strong>Protected Area</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Description</strong></p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>National Parks</p>",
            "<p>Strictly protected areas where wildlife and habitat are fully protected; no human activity allowed</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Wildlife Sanctuaries</p>",
            "<p>Areas where animals are protected but limited human activities may be allowed</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Biosphere Reserves</p>",
            "<p>Large areas protecting biodiversity, ecosystems and traditional communities</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Tiger Reserves</p>",
            "<p>Special reserves created under Project Tiger to conserve tigers</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Bird Sanctuaries</p>",
            "<p>Protected areas mainly for migratory and native birds</p>"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
